   You may download and use the Software for personal play.


2. PACK CONTENT GRANT

   Create: Gunpowder adds a production chain that pack authors are expected to
   rebalance, extend, or switch off. Nothing in Section 1 is intended to
   restrict that, and this section grants the rights needed to do it.

   "Pack Content" means data and assets loaded at runtime by Minecraft, the mod
   loader, or another mod: datapacks, resource packs, recipe and tag overrides,
   KubeJS or CraftTweaker scripts, configuration files, and similar files that
   contain no part of the Software's own code or assets.

   You are granted a perpetual, worldwide, royalty-free, irrevocable right to:

   (a) Create Pack Content that adds to, alters, overrides, or disables
       Create: Gunpowder's recipes, tags, items, and other registry entries,
       for any purpose, including commercial purposes.

   (b) Distribute, sell, and license your Pack Content on any terms you choose,
       through any channel.

   (c) Use Create: Gunpowder's registry identifiers, item and tag names, recipe
       definitions, translation keys, and directory layouts for the purpose of
       authoring Pack Content or interoperating with the Software.

   (d) Write separate mods, tools, editors, validators, or libraries that
       interoperate with Create: Gunpowder through its registry entries or its
       recipe and tag definitions.

   You own your Pack Content. This license claims no ownership over, and
   imposes no licensing terms on, content you create. Overriding or extending
   Create: Gunpowder's recipes does not make your work a derivative work of the
   Software, and no attribution to Create: Gunpowder is required.

   This grant is irrevocable: it cannot be withdrawn from Pack Content already
   published, and it survives any future change to this license.


3. LIMITS OF THE GRANT

   Section 2 does not permit you to:

   (a) Redistribute the Software's own code, binaries, or bundled assets,
       whether modified or unmodified, except as allowed in Section 4.

   (b) Present Pack Content, or any other work, in a way that implies it is
       Create: Gunpowder itself, or that it is endorsed by or affiliated with
       the project.


4. MODPACK INCLUSION

   You may include Create: Gunpowder in a modpack, free or paid, provided that
   all of the following hold:

   (a) The modpack uses a distribution format that fetches Create: Gunpowder
       from an official distribution page operated or authorised by the
       copyright holder. The end user's launcher performs the download; the
       modpack itself carries a reference, not the file. CurseForge manifests
       and Modrinth .mrpack index entries are the intended examples.

   (b) The modpack does not bundle, mirror, re-host, or otherwise include a
       copy of the Create: Gunpowder JAR.

   (c) Create: Gunpowder is distributed unmodified. You may not patch,
       repackage, strip, recompile, or alter the JAR in any way.

   (d) Configuration files and Pack Content shipped alongside are unaffected by
       this section and remain governed by Section 2.

   This permission is automatically revoked for any modpack that breaches (a)
   through (c).


